{"max_tokens":8192,"messages":[{"content":"{\"schema_version\": 7, \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_d0889cdfc8704adc\", \"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"response_pilot_17\", \"approved_glossary\": {\"LT\": \"Label Tool, the internal labeling platform\", \"QN\": \"Quarantine\", \"TL\": \"Team Lead\", \"QA\": \"Quality Assurance or QA Tutor depending on context\", \"L0\": \"Initial labeling layer / first-pass labelers\", \"queue\": \"Batch of assigned labeling tasks\", \"tasking\": \"Actively completing labeling tasks\", \"align\": \"Clarify a rule so labeling behavior becomes consistent\", \"flag\": \"Raise an issue for review\", \"rubric\": \"Evaluation or scoring criteria\"}, \"members\": [{\"member_id\": \"member_87f955f0c95aa5bc22870168\", \"summary\": \"Casey Tran (TUTOR) reported that Candidate B has two extra blank lines between bullets, that the two answers otherwise say exactly the same thing, and that there is no output format restriction, and asked whether to prefer A. Noah Bell (QA_TUTOR) replied to pick Tie, because extra whitespace alone does not affect preference when there is no format requirement. A TEAM_LEAD (U9103) endorsed that reply with a white_check_mark reaction.\", \"central_question\": \"Given two answers that are identical in content except that Candidate B has two extra blank lines between bullets, and no output format restriction, should the preference go to Candidate A?\"}, {\"member_id\": \"member_b82cc19fe1fa9c4e46c179d0\", \"summary\": \"Jamie Park (TUTOR) asked whether a difference in leading whitespace changes the label when two otherwise identical answers differ only in that one begins with a blank line. Sam Vega (TEAM_LEAD) replied that Tie should be used for this item because the task does not specify exact serialization.\", \"central_question\": \"For two otherwise identical answers where one begins with a blank line and the other does not, does that difference change the preference label?\"}]}","role":"